---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = "Estimating PMI Cost (Monthly Mortgage Insurance)";
const description =
  "Estimate PMI cost and understand how it affects your monthly payment and removal timeline. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-05";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/guides/estimating-pmi-cost"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  robots="noindex, follow"
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview, TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview]}
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">PMI cost</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Estimating PMI cost</h1>
    <p>
      PMI is usually required when your down payment is below 20%. This guide shows how to estimate the monthly PMI cost and
      how it fits into your housing payment.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/pmi-removal-vs-extra-principal">PMI removal vs extra principal</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    reviewScope="Monthly PMI estimate realism, monthly-versus-upfront mortgage insurance interpretation, and routing between mortgage payment, PMI thresholds, and removal workflows."
    reviewedOn="2026-04-05"
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when PMI cost is the missing piece of the full housing-payment estimate</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when principal and interest look fine, but the monthly payment still feels incomplete because PMI has not been estimated realistically.</li>
      <li>If you need to see when PMI applies or ends, move next to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-pmi-thresholds">PMI thresholds and mortgage payments</a>.</li>
      <li>If your next decision is whether faster extra principal is better than waiting for removal, move next to <a href="/guides/pmi-removal-vs-extra-principal">PMI removal vs extra principal</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Mortgage payment inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount, note rate, and term.</li>
      <li>Taxes, insurance, HOA, and PMI assumptions.</li>
      <li>Escrow rules or reserves used by the lender.</li>
      <li>Time horizon if comparing scenarios.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">When PMI applies</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      PMI is commonly required on conventional loans when your down payment is below 20% of the purchase price. The rules vary
      by loan type, credit profile, and lender.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to estimate PMI</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Ask your lender for the estimated PMI rate.</li>
      <li>Multiply the loan amount by the PMI rate to get the annual cost.</li>
      <li>Divide by 12 to get the monthly PMI amount.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">PMI removal timing</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      PMI can typically be removed once your loan reaches a certain loan-to-value threshold, but the rules depend on your loan
      terms and payment history. Extra principal can accelerate that timeline.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Using a generic PMI rate instead of a lender quote.</li>
      <li>Ignoring PMI when estimating the housing payment and DTI.</li>
      <li>Assuming PMI removal is automatic without confirming the lender process.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Expected credit score band for the quote.</li>
      <li>Loan-to-value at purchase and at expected removal.</li>
      <li>Whether PMI is monthly or upfront.</li>
      <li>Appraisal cost and timing for removal requests.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">Extra payment calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/pmi-removal-vs-extra-principal">PMI removal vs extra principal</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">How mortgage payments are calculated</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Does PMI apply to FHA loans?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      FHA loans use a different type of mortgage insurance with different rules. Ask your lender how it will be calculated.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can I remove PMI early?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      You may be able to request removal once you meet the loan-to-value threshold. Confirm the lender requirements and timing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/when-can-i-remove-private-mortgage-insurance-pmi-from-my-loan-en-202/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          When can I remove private mortgage insurance (PMI) from my loan?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/ready-to-buy-a-home/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Ready to buy a home?
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Run the mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/pmi-removal-vs-extra-principal">PMI removal guide</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-05</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>



